1
00:00:06,447 --> 00:00:07,867
(Stuart:)- Hey, Leonard.
- Oh, hi.

2
00:00:08,032 --> 00:00:09,452
- How's it going?
- Good, good.

3
00:00:09,617 --> 00:00:11,497
(Leonard:)- You?
- Fine.

4
00:00:11,661 --> 00:00:14,581
- Oh, yeah, hey, can I ask you something?
- Sure.

5
00:00:15,039 --> 00:00:16,329
(Penny:)You know your friend Stuart?

6
00:00:17,041 --> 00:00:18,711
(Sheldon:)Yes.

7
00:00:19,001 --> 00:00:21,211
(Penny:)Well, he asked me out again
and I said yes.

8
00:00:21,379 --> 00:00:24,339
(Penny:)And then I started thinking
maybe I should talk to you first.

9
00:00:24,507 --> 00:00:26,797
- About what?
- Well, does it bother you?

10
00:00:26,968 --> 00:00:28,718
(Penny:)Me going out with one of your friends?

11
00:00:28,886 --> 00:00:33,306
- Because, you know, you and me...
- No. No, that's the past.

12
00:00:33,474 --> 00:00:35,434
(Leonard:)I'm really more of a right now
kind of guy.

13
00:00:35,601 --> 00:00:37,851
(Leonard:)You know, living in the moment.

14
00:00:38,396 --> 00:00:42,066
(Leonard:)Although I do have to live a little
in the future because, well, that's my job.

15
00:00:42,566 --> 00:00:46,566
(Leonard:)Of course, my fondness for classic science
fiction does draw my attention backwards...

16
00:00:46,737 --> 00:00:49,577
(Leonard:)...but those stories often take place
in the future, so...

17
00:00:52,159 --> 00:00:54,039
(Leonard:)In conclusion, no, it doesn't bother me.

18
00:00:56,163 --> 00:00:58,043
(Penny:)Okay, well, that's really cool of you.

19
00:00:58,207 --> 00:01:00,337
LEONARD:
Yeah? Well, I wouldn't say cool.

20
00:01:00,501 --> 00:01:04,021
I'd just say, "That's Leonard."

